0.1.1  2026-11-14
     - fixed repeated zero-width line-end searches remaining on the current line
     - added forward, wrapping and reverse line-end search regression tests

0.1.0  2026-11-14
     - initial human-testing prerelease: a single-file Perl-centric vi-style editor
     - targets Perl 5.10+ with core-only runtime dependencies and no privileged install
     - added disk-backed line index, edit pieces, bounded cache and streaming saves
     - added normal/insert/replace modes, counts, navigation, paging and line numbers
     - added line/character yank and put, delete/change, joins, undo and redo
     - added forward/backward Perl-regex search and ranged s/// with g/i and captures
     - added approximate Perl syntax colors and optional undoable perltidy -l 500
     - added POD, CLI help/manual, batch commands and provisional startup splash
     - added guarded atomic saves and byte/newline preservation
     - added model-based, command, CLI, optional tidy and real PTY integration tests
     - added cross-platform/version CI, benchmarks and gated prerelease packaging
